THE MAHARASHTRA REAL ESTATE REGULATORY AUTHORITY,
MUMBAI.COMPLAINT NO: CC006000000078S30
Pankaj Mar-rohar Bhargalkar.VersusM/s. Om sai Infi'a & Om sai Group.(Sai Kanishk l,hase lI)MahaRERA Regn: P51700012436.Coram:
Complainant
. . Respondents
Shri B.D. Kapadnis,Hon'ble Member II.
Appearance:Complainant: Inperson.Respondents: Absent.
Final Order9tt'october 2019.
The complainant has filed this complaint under section 1g of RERA forclaiming interest on his investment for delayed possession and under section 19 (3)for claiming possession of his booked flat no.707, Building No. 8-6, Florida, saiKanishk situated at Village Dawle, Diva.2. The complainant relies upon the agreement for sale which shows that therespondents agreed to hand over the possession of his booked flat on or beforeDecember 2018. It is also mentioned therein that if the respondents fail to hand overthe possession of the booked flat on said date, there shall be the reasonable extensionof 12 months. Thus, the agreed date of possession is December 2019 which has notbeen crossed. Hence, i find that the complainant has no cause of action to claim relief
under Section 18 & 19.3. The complaint is dismissed.
Place: Mumbai.Date: 09.10.2019.
q.
o
(8.D. Kapadnis).. Member II,MahaRERA, Mumbai.
\
oI
\

endstream
